  clock: 3  # 188a
  nonce: 188a  # 188a
  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, deeper-issue investigation): reproduced on gitleaks v8.30.0 — `gitleaks detect --no-git --pipe` returns `INF scanned ~0 bytes` and `[]` when given a known AWS-key string on stdin, confirming the --pipe regression. The whole test_gitleaks.py file mocks subprocess.run, so a real-binary smoke test on a known-positive string would have flagged the v8.30 contract break immediately. Same fail-silent-on-external-dep pattern as the umbrella INV-fabov names for argparse/YAML inputs; here the silent layer is subprocess output instead. Suggested follow-up to consider when fixing: gitleaks 8.x prefers `gitleaks stdin` (new subcommand) or `gitleaks detect --source -` for stdin scanning; verify the working invocation against a known-positive fixture in a non-mocked test before re-enabling in the cache path."  # 188a
